The primary objective of this research paper is to outline the key objectives and potential future developments of the Dark-matter And neutrino Computation Explored (DANCE) collaboration. This community-driven project aims to advance our understanding of dark matter and neutrinos through cutting-edge scientific inquiry and collaborative research. Leveraging the strengths of high-performance computing, the DANCE initiative addresses pressing scientific questions and seeks to develop new technologies to detect these elusive particles. With a diverse range of expertise, the DANCE community is uniquely positioned to contribute to the advancement of both dark matter and neutrino detection strategies. This contribution provides a comprehensive overview of the DANCE collaboration's goals, scientific objectives, and technical approaches, as well as its potential contributions to the field of particle astrophysics and cosmology. Additionally, the document provides a list of specific research initiatives and funding requirements for the DANCE community to support its research endeavors. Finally, the document concludes with a list of recommendations and proposed actions for the advancement of the DANCE collaboration. Download links for relevant supporting materials are available online. More detailed information on the DANCE collaboration can be found on the project's website. \bigskip \par

